                <p rendition="#flush">I <hi rendition="#italic">Deputies Report and Agenda</hi></p>
                <p>The Council heard the Deputies’ Report, presented by the Chairman of the day.</p>
                <p>The Council decided to examine first of all the question of the Peace Conference
                    (draft invitations and rules of procedure), next the question of Italian
                    reparation (final text) and then the question of Germany.</p>
                <p>The questions appearing in point 3 of document CFM (46) 191<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d245-f1"/> were referred back to the Deputies, who should report
                    whether or not they had been able to reach an agreement on these various
                    points.</p>
                <pb facs="0825" n="801" xml:id="pg801"/>
                <p rendition="#flush">II <hi rendition="#italic">Peace Conference</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Draft Invitations and Rules of Procedure</hi>)</p>
                <p>After an exchange of views on this question, the Council instructed the Deputies
                    to resume study of the matter on the following day, July 6, at 10:00 a.m. and
                    report to the Council on its afternoon meeting.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">III <hi rendition="#italic">Reparation Due From Italy</hi></p>
                <p>The Council instructed the Deputies to draw up, in accordance with the
                    instructions given them at the 34th meeting of the Council, a complete document
                    on reparation from Italy which would include a reference to the claims of Allied
                    nations other than the U.S.S.R. and which would be submitted to the Council at
                    the next meeting.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">IV <hi rendition="#italic">Next Meeting of the
                    Council</hi></p>
                <p>Saturday, July 6, at 4:00 p.m.</p>
